    "title": "Man killed in shooting at northeast Kansas City apartment Wednesday night - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Caroline Zimmerman ,\n1 hours ago\nMan killed in shooting at northeast Kansas City apartment Wednesday night A man is dead following a shooting Wednesday nightat a northeast Kansas City apartment.\nKansas City police officers were dispatched to the 500 block of Bales Avenue just before 6:30 p.m. Wednesday on a medical call, according to a press release from Kansas City Police Department spokesperson Officer Alayna Gonzalez.\nParamedics were already at the scene when officers arrived, Gonzalez said, and advised officers that an unresponsive man was inside an apartment.\nFurther investigation revealed the man was suffering from gunshot trauma, Gonzalez said. He was pronounced dead at the scene.\nNo suspects have been identified, and it’s unclear what circumstances led to the shooting, Gonzalez said.\nThe shooting marks the 110th homicide in Kansas City in 2025, compared to 109 at this time last year , according to data tracked by The Star ; which includes police-involved shootings.\nGonzalez said anyone with information regarding the incident should contact homicide detectives at 816-234-5043, or contact the TIPS hotline at 816-474-TIPS. All tips submitted to the TIPS hotline remain anonymous and are eligible for a reward up to $25,000.",
